{
  "id": "consolidation-hypothesis",
  "term": "consolidation hypothesis",
  "definition": "The consolidation hypothesis is the idea that emotion strengthens the later feeling of recollection because emotional experiences undergo a time-dependent memory-consolidation process that relies importantly on the hippocampus. In this view, the emotional advantage in recollective experience becomes more noticeable after a delay and is reduced when hippocampal function is impaired.",
